WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:00.840
All right, friends.

00:00.840 --> 00:02.560
So now let's switch to ChatGPT.

00:02.760 --> 00:08.360
So let's start first by understanding the structure and the basic components of ChatGPT prompts.

00:12.400 --> 00:16.200
So the first component and the most important one we have the tasks.

00:16.200 --> 00:19.720
You have to be very clear by defining what the AI should do.

00:19.720 --> 00:23.880
And without having a clear tasks the AI will not understand what to do.

00:23.880 --> 00:26.840
So this is mandatory in each prompts.

00:26.840 --> 00:29.800
And then after that you have to provide some context.

00:29.800 --> 00:31.680
So you give some background information.

00:31.680 --> 00:36.240
Like for example you say I am students or I am a data engineer and so on.

00:36.360 --> 00:39.720
And another component we have to add specifications.

00:39.720 --> 00:43.160
So in the task you give the main task what the AI should do.

00:43.160 --> 00:48.720
But with the specifications you go in details like for example which topic should be added or maybe

00:48.720 --> 00:51.640
excluded the number of word counts.

00:51.840 --> 00:57.640
So here you are specifying a lot of wishes and small details and specifications in order to get an answer

00:57.640 --> 00:59.400
that meets your expectations.

00:59.400 --> 01:02.960
So both of their contexts and specifications, they are important.

01:02.960 --> 01:07.960
And then after that we have some nice to have components like for example specifying a rule.

01:07.960 --> 01:09.970
So here you give the I a rule.

01:09.970 --> 01:14.250
Like for example, you tell it to act as an expert as a teacher.

01:14.290 --> 01:15.250
Interviewer.

01:15.450 --> 01:18.250
So you are setting the AI to play a rule.

01:18.250 --> 01:21.130
And the last component that you can add is as well the tone.

01:21.170 --> 01:26.730
Here you are defining like the voice of the answer in order just to make the answer like more friendly

01:26.730 --> 01:28.770
and easy to read and engaging.

01:28.850 --> 01:31.370
So the role and the tone, they are nice to have.

01:31.410 --> 01:36.290
And if you go and use all those components, you will get a better result from the AI.

01:36.570 --> 01:41.170
So let's take for example the following prompts explain SQL window functions.

01:41.250 --> 01:43.450
So this is very simple and very short.

01:43.650 --> 01:46.530
And here we have only one component the task.

01:46.570 --> 01:51.730
So here you are not giving any context whether it is for data analytics or for data engineering.

01:51.850 --> 01:53.690
So you leave it up to the AI.

01:53.810 --> 01:57.770
And maybe the answer that you will get will not meet the expectation that you have.

01:57.810 --> 02:02.090
And now if you want to shape it in the way that you want, you have to add more components.

02:02.130 --> 02:06.610
Like for example, this prompts you are saying you are a senior SQL expert.

02:06.650 --> 02:09.530
So here we are defining the rule for the AI.

02:09.650 --> 02:12.730
So the AI should act now as an SQL expert.

02:12.730 --> 02:16.290
And then the next section we are adding a context to the prompts.

02:16.330 --> 02:20.790
So we are saying I'm a data analyst working on SQL projects using SQL server.

02:20.790 --> 02:26.270
So now the answer that you will get from the I going to use the syntax of the SQL server and focus on

02:26.270 --> 02:27.590
the topic of analytics.

02:27.590 --> 02:29.910
That's why the context is very important.

02:29.910 --> 02:33.230
And then we go specify in the prompt the task the main task.

02:33.230 --> 02:37.430
So we say explain the concept of SQL window functions and do the following.

02:37.470 --> 02:42.590
And now we go and give more fine details about what the I should provide.

02:42.590 --> 02:47.950
We are saying explain each window function and show the syntax, describe why they are important and

02:47.950 --> 02:51.430
when to use them, and list the top three use cases.

02:51.430 --> 02:55.310
So you are now specifying what you are expecting from the I.

02:55.510 --> 03:00.630
And after that, of course, it is nice to have we specify the tone of the explanation.

03:00.630 --> 03:06.590
So we say the tone should be conversational and direct, as if you are speaking to me 1 to 1, so that

03:06.590 --> 03:09.030
it is not like you are reading a document.

03:09.030 --> 03:11.350
You are reading something that is engaging.

03:11.350 --> 03:17.750
So I know this prompt is really big, but still you will get way better results than only saying explain

03:17.750 --> 03:18.750
the concepts.

03:18.750 --> 03:21.150
So those are the main components that I usually use.

03:21.150 --> 03:25.630
If I'm starting like a conversation and a discussion with the ChatGPT.
